WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.267 --> 00:00:16.671
"Second star to the right and then straight on till morning."

2
00:00:16.672 --> 00:00:20.686
That was how Peter had described the way to the island of Neverland.

3
00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:26.297
But these directions were not very exact. And the children had no map!

4
00:00:26.298 --> 00:00:30.239
They were depending on Peter to guide them there.

5
00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.665
At first, they were excited as he led them through the clouds.

6
00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:43.826
They flew over treetops, made rings around tall buildings, and dipped close to the waves in the sea.

7
00:00:43.827 --> 00:00:50.037
From the sky, the world looked very different and their eyes delighted in everything.

8
00:00:50.038 --> 00:00:55.824
"Follow me!" Peter commanded. He used his best captain's voice.

9
00:00:55.825 --> 00:00:58.947
But Peter was a little too daring.

10
00:00:58.948 --> 00:01:04.138
He flew a little too close to the trees―just missing their branches.

11
00:01:04.139 --> 00:01:09.735
He flew a little too close to the water—touching every shark's tail.

12
00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:19.128
As the children flew with Peter, night became day, light became dark; then it became light, then dark again.

13
00:01:19.129 --> 00:01:22.831
The moon and the sun took turns trading places.

14
00:01:22.832 --> 00:01:26.659
The children followed Peter bravely.

15
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:30.037
But the excitement of flying started to wear off.

16
00:01:30.038 --> 00:01:32.789
The children became hungry and cold.

17
00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:37.419
They also became sleepy, and this was dangerous.

18
00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.945
In order to fly, they had to remain awake.

19
00:01:40.946 --> 00:01:46.043
When Michael suddenly nodded off, he began to fall.

20
00:01:46.044 --> 00:01:52.275
"There he goes—down, down, down!" Peter laughed.

21
00:01:52.276 --> 00:01:56.417
He thought this was hilarious, but Wendy was alarmed.

22
00:01:56.418 --> 00:02:00.209
Peter caught Michael just before he fell into the sea.

23
00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:07.378
When he saw how upset Wendy was, he taught the children how to rest on a cloud.

24
00:02:07.379 --> 00:02:10.405
Peter flew much faster than the others.

25
00:02:10.406 --> 00:02:13.346
Sometimes he would fly out of sight for a while.

26
00:02:13.347 --> 00:02:16.029
He had secret adventures on his own.

27
00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:20.006
He would come back talking about a star or a fairy he had met.

28
00:02:20.007 --> 00:02:25.660
When he was out on an adventure, Wendy worried that he might forget them altogether!

29
00:02:25.661 --> 00:02:30.783
"What would we do if Peter were to leave us?" asked John.

30
00:02:30.784 --> 00:02:33.446
"Well, we would have to go on.

31
00:02:33.447 --> 00:02:38.890
We don't know how to stop," replied Wendy, trying to sound brave.

32
00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:44.108
This was true. Peter had not shown them how to stop flying.

33
00:02:44.109 --> 00:02:48.354
Soon they lost track of time. How long had they been traveling?

34
00:02:48.355 --> 00:02:51.046
Would they ever arrive in Neverland?

35
00:02:51.047 --> 00:02:54.348
The children wondered whether they had lost their way.

36
00:02:54.349 --> 00:02:58.188
Finally, they saw an island in the distance.

37
00:02:58.189 --> 00:03:00.903
The island seemed to be calling to them.

38
00:03:00.904 --> 00:03:06.534
It was all very new and strange—yet somehow familiar at the same time.

39
00:03:06.535 --> 00:03:11.812
"There it is," said Peter, "where all the arrows are pointing."

40
00:03:11.813 --> 00:03:13.295
He was right.

41
00:03:13.296 --> 00:03:19.280
A hundred golden arrows, sent by the setting sun, pointed to the magic shore of Neverland.

42
00:03:19.281 --> 00:03:21.667
Night was approaching.

43
00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:25.276
The sun wanted to make sure they found their way safely.

44
00:03:25.277 --> 00:03:30.681
The children looked down below. They could see splashes of color everywhere.

45
00:03:30.682 --> 00:03:34.316
Purple mountains stood behind dark green forests.

46
00:03:34.317 --> 00:03:38.690
Rivers and lakes ran through the green land like blue veins.

47
00:03:38.691 --> 00:03:42.246
Red coral reefs accented the color of the water.

48
00:03:42.247 --> 00:03:47.157
Flowers and bushes in brilliant shades dotted the landscape of Neverland.

49
00:03:47.158 --> 00:03:51.522
Strangely, the children immediately recognized the island.

50
00:03:51.523 --> 00:03:56.071
Below them, they each saw a landscape from their own dreams.

51
00:03:56.072 --> 00:03:59.005
John saw his lake with flamingos.

52
00:03:59.006 --> 00:04:02.618
Michael saw his cave with a river running through it.

53
00:04:02.619 --> 00:04:07.261
And Wendy saw Mermaid Lagoon, just as she had often dreamed of it.

54
00:04:07.262 --> 00:04:12.062
In the nursery, Neverland had been make-believe, part of a dream world.

55
00:04:12.063 --> 00:04:15.909
Now that they were here, it was all very real.

56
00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:20.678
The sun's golden arrows disappeared; the sky became dark.

57
00:04:20.679 --> 00:04:25.951
Night was falling on Neverland, and suddenly the children were frightened.

58
00:04:25.952 --> 00:04:29.427
There were no nursery night-lights to keep them safe.

59
00:04:29.428 --> 00:04:32.281
Nana wasn't standing guard beside them.

60
00:04:32.282 --> 00:04:40.499
Still flying, they all moved closer to Peter.
